5d0bc665e9aace17cc093a4d6b629290b1946055.text:
{
  "summary": "IMF staff observe that safe-haven demand into Switzerland primarily targets bank deposits due to its small US$150 billion debt market, compared to US$35 trillion in the US and US$9 trillion in Japan. Historically accommodated by SNB interventions—such as during the euro area debt crisis, where nonresidents accumulated CHF 132 billion in bank accounts—inflows and interventions declined in 2025. IMF staff warn this shift creates a new risk environment where safe-haven flows could heighten financial market volatility and expand domestic bank lending."
}

